A command answered before its clip shows does not show it.

The page's VNAS window waits 4 s for a command's clip to start and then
answers VNAS failed/timeout, but the card's own fetch limit is 10 s, so a clip
that came later still showed: the pet did what VNAS had been told it did not
do. The card now asks the page (playbackSettled) before a command's clip goes
in and again before it shows. A clip the command started is dropped and the
chain goes on from the clip in front, as after a command's clip that did not
play; a clip the chain was loading anyway, which the command took over, shows
without the command.

